weighed:
No shaking of my hand disturbed the poise;
Weighed, found it wanting: not a word I said,
But silent made my choice.

These long patrician hands, clasping the crucifix,
Show she had weighed the world, her will was set;
These pale curved lips of hers, holding their hidden smile,

When ghostly lanes turn toward the shadowy morn;
When bodies weighed with satiate passion's power
Sad, disappointed from each other turn;

weigh:
I tell you I am what I was and more.
My branches weigh me down, frost cleans the air,
My sky is black with small birds bearing south;

weighty:
'Then men were men of might and right,
Sheer might, at least, and weighty swords;
Then men in open blood and fire,

weird:
Night jasmines cannot bloom in this cold place;
Without the street is wet and weird with snow;
The cold nude trees are tossing to and fro;

Like a soul gone mad with pain
I must match its weird refrain;
Ever must I twist and squirm,

weirdest:
Come the purple flowers, opium filled,
From which the weirdest myths are distilled;
My orient porcelains contain them all.

weighs:
With analytic eyes;
I wonder if it weighs like mine,
Or has an easier size.

weigh'd:
A spear he proudly wav'd, whose iron head,
Strange to relate, six hundred shekels weigh'd;
He strode along, and shook the ample field,

weightless:
It levelled strong Euphrates in its course;
Supreme yet weightless as an idle mote
It seemed to tame the waters without force
